        "note": "panel_mission carries its own disableAfterDelay: disableDelay 3.8, enabled, targeting itself, at PlayerShip_SR14_Photon.prefab:10176 and :12320, mechanism in disableAfterDelay.cs:8-16. disableDelay is a public float with NO initialiser, so 3.8 is shipped behaviour and not a code default. A panel live at spawn (see liveAtSpawn above) is therefore killed 3.8 s after spawn; one that is not does not start its countdown until something activates it, because Start() does not run on an inactive GameObject. What activates it, if anything, is NOT traced here. HUD_Ship.DelayedStart (HUD_Ship.cs:88-99) then hides it a SECOND time at 0.12+4=4.12 s, against a panel already inactive for 0.32 s. 4.12 is real but it is NOT the figure: DEV-200 made that trade on the strength of a citation pointing at HUD_Ship.cs rather than at the prefab, and DEV-217 undid it. Ends in a newline, which is in the shipped bytes."
